During the bootstrap-driven configure of the full CMake, the minimal
stage-1 cmake does not populate CMAKE_SYSTEM_NAME, so the GHS generator
sources are gated out. cmake.cxx however references them unconditionally
whenever __linux__ (or _WIN32) is defined, producing undefined-reference
link errors (seen with host GCC 16). Gate on "NOT APPLE" instead, which
does not depend on CMAKE_SYSTEM_NAME being detected and matches the C++
preprocessor condition (linux/windows = include, apple = exclude).

--- a/Source/CMakeLists.txt
+++ b/Source/CMakeLists.txt
@@ -951,7 +951,7 @@ endif()

 # GHS support
 # Works only for windows and linux
-if(WIN32 OR CMAKE_SYSTEM_NAME STREQUAL "Linux")
+if(WIN32 OR NOT APPLE)
   target_sources(
     CMakeLib
     PRIVATE
